Usage: fmt [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Reformat paragraphs.

With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

Note: This is a simplified implementation. Advanced features
like crown margin and tagged paragraphs are not fully supported.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --crown-margin       preserve indentation of the first two lines
  -m, --preserve-headers   attempt to detect and preserve mail headers
  -p, --prefix ARG         reformat only lines beginning with STRING
  -P, --skip-prefix ARG    do not reformat lines beginning with STRING
  -s, --split-only         split long lines, but do not refill
  -t, --tagged-paragraph   expect indentation in first 2 lines
  -u, --uniform-spacing    one space between words, two after sentences
  -x, --exact-prefix       do not ignore leading whitespace for -p
  -X, --exact-skip-prefix  do not ignore leading whitespace for -P
  -T, --tab-width ARG      treat tabs as TABWIDTH spaces when measuring line
                           length
  -w, --width ARG          maximum line width (default 75)
  -g, --goal ARG           goal width (default 93% of width)
      --help               display this help and exit
  -V, --version            output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
